{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"openWorldHint":true,"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"Who sells a model, and at what price. Most models are sold by several hosts (the model maker, a cloud platform such as Amazon Bedrock, Azure or Vertex, or an independent host) at different rates, and every other tool here quotes ONE of them. For 1-4 named models this returns how many hosts sell each, the cheapest, the dearest, the model maker's own rate, the spread between them, any promotional listing, and what a workload costs per request and per month at each. Use it for 'where is Llama 3.3 70B cheapest', 'is the price you quoted the maker's own', 'how much does the choice of host matter for this model'. To cost a workload at the quoted price with caching and batch, use estimate-llm-cost. Read the caveats it returns: the cheapest host may serve a quantized build, which is not the same product, or a promotional rate that ends. It also lists every host with its rate, cheapest first, the platforms the model is listed on (Direct API, AWS Bedrock, Azure AI Foundry, Google Vertex, OpenRouter: a hand-kept estimate for the major models) and the AWS regions where Amazon Bedrock lists it. `hostList.available` says whether that full list was read: without it only the cheapest, the dearest, the maker's own and promotional listings are known, and the text says so. A missing platform or region is not known, never 'not sold there'. Per-host prices are list prices read nightly and dated by `provenance.hostPricingAsOf`, and a model with no host data says so rather than reading as sold by one host.","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","properties":{"models":{"description":"1-4 model names, e.g. ['Llama 3.3 70B'] or ['Claude Sonnet 5', 'DeepSeek V4']","items":{"type":"string"},"maxItems":4,"minItems":1,"type":"array"},"useCasePreset":{"description":"Workload the costs are computed for, which sets tokens per request: 